<!-- ===== QA program ===== -->
<section class="px-block soft">
  <div class="ht-wrap">
    <div class="px-sec-head px-reveal">
      <div class="px-kicker">Nuclear Quality Assurance Program</div>
      <h2>QA isn't a checklist here. It's the operating system.</h2>
      <p>Nuclear supply chain quality requirements exist because the cost of a field failure &mdash; in dose exposure, downtime, regulatory scrutiny, and schedule &mdash; is orders of magnitude higher than the cost of getting it right in the shop. Harris Thermal has an NQA-1 quality assurance program in place, built on the quality systems that have supported regulated projects throughout our history. Contact our quality team to discuss project-specific qualification needs. Our <a href="/quality-control-safety/">quality control and inspection program</a> and <a href="/certifications/">current certifications</a> set out what we hold and how equipment is examined, tested and documented.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="px-mats px-reveal"><h3>Quality System Framework</h3><ul>
<li>Controlled document &amp; drawing revision system &mdash; every record tied to an approved revision</li>
<li>Material traceability to heat and lot &mdash; MTRs linked to specific weld joints and components</li>
<li>Qualified welding procedures &amp; current welder qualification records</li>
<li>In-process inspection hold points with documented sign-off</li>
<li>Non-conformance reports with documented disposition &mdash; no verbal waivers</li>
<li>Final documentation packages: MTRs, weld maps, NDE, hydro test, QC sign-offs</li>
<li>Supplier qualification process for nuclear-grade procurements</li>
<li>Audit-ready records retention aligned with NQA-1 requirements</li>
</ul></div>
    <div class="px-sec-head px-reveal" style="margin:44px auto 0">
      <p>When you source a component from a shop with a mature nuclear quality assurance program, you're not just buying a piece of metal &mdash; you're buying a documentation trail that can survive a regulatory audit, an owner's inspection, and a design review years after delivery. <strong>Harris Thermal's NQA-1 quality assurance program is built on that foundation.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="px-callout px-reveal" style="margin-top:44px">
      <div>
        <div class="px-kicker" style="color:#7db4f7">Technical Reading</div>
        <h3>Nuclear process equipment fabrication: NQA-1 quality assurance and traceability</h3>
        <p>What an NQA-1 program actually governs, how traceability flows from heat number to weld joint, and why a Code stamp and a nuclear quality program are two different things.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <a class="px-btn px-btn-primary" href="/2026/08/17/nuclear-process-equipment-fabrication-nqa-1-quality-assurance-and-traceability/">Read the article</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

